#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:1
msgid "Contributing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:3
msgid "Contribution Guidelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:5
msgid ""
"You don’t need to know how to code to contribute to Open Data Editor, you"
" just need time and attitude. There are many possible ways to contribute "
"to the project:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:7
msgid "Use the Open Data Editor and give us feedback"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:8
msgid "Spread the word about it\\!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:9
msgid "Improve the documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:10
msgid "Add a translation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:11
msgid "Report issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:12
msgid "Contribute to the code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:14
msgid "Please read this guide for more details on the contribution process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:16
msgid "How can you help?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:18
msgid "Giving us feedback"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:20
msgid ""
"Use the Open Data Editor and give us feedback. You can try out all the "
"features and report any issues you might encounter. You can also suggest "
"improvements to the Open Data Editor’s look and layout. For example, *if "
"something feels confusing or hard to find in the tool’s layout, you can "
"suggest changes to make it easier to use.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:22
msgid ""
"Feedback from a beginner’s perspective is particularly welcome as it "
"helps us improve usability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:24
msgid ""
"To give us feedback, you can either [open an issue in the GitHub "
"repository](https://github.com/okfn/opendataeditor) or reach out by email"
" at info@okfn.org."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:26
msgid "Spread the word"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:28
msgid ""
"If you like the application, tell others about it\\! Spreading the word "
"about the Open Data Editor is also a valuable contribution to the "
"project. Whether you share it on social media, write a blog post, create "
"a tutorial video, or simply tell a friend, you’re helping more people "
"discover and use the tool. Every bit of awareness and engagement makes a "
"difference\\!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:30
msgid "Documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:32
msgid "Improving documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:34
msgid ""
"Documentation is always the best place to start contributing. If you spot"
" a typo or you’ve ever thought, “I wish the documentation explained this "
"more clearly,” you can help make it easier to understand. You can either "
"flag that, or propose a modification. You can also add missing steps or "
"explanations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:36
msgid "Adding examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:38
msgid ""
"You can also contribute by adding examples\\! If you notice something is "
"not covered in the documentation, try creating a helpful example and "
"sharing it. You can also provide real-world use cases to show how Open "
"Data Editor can be used. Every improvement makes Open Data Editor easier "
"for everyone to use\\!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:40
msgid ""
"All documentation files are contained [in this "
"folder](https://github.com/okfn/opendataeditor/tree/main/portal/content/docs/documentation)."
" You can just propose a change or add examples by opening a PR. Please "
"**always include a short description of what you changed and why**, so it"
" is easier to review. If you don’t feel comfortable using GitHub, you can"
" also send us an email with the proposed changes at info\\[at\\]okfn.org."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:42
msgid "Use cases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:44
msgid ""
"If you have started using Open Data Editor in your daily work and would "
"like to share with the world how the tool is helping you, you can always "
"write a blog about it. You can find a few examples "
"[here](https://blog.okfn.org/tag/ode-use-cases/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:46
msgid ""
"If possible, try to include photos and screenshots. If you need guidance,"
" you can always reach out to us at info@okfn.org. You can send us your "
"blog at that same email address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:48
msgid "Reporting a bug"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:50
msgid ""
"We use GitHub as a code and issues hosting platform. To report a bug or "
"propose a new feature, please open an issue [in the "
"repository](https://github.com/okfn/opendataeditor/issues). Please "
"provide a detailed description of the bug and include screenshots. There "
"are a few predefined issue templates to help you get started."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:52
msgid ""
"If you don’t feel comfortable using GitHub, you can also send us an email"
" at info@okfn.org."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:54
msgid "Code contributions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:56
msgid "Pull requests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:58
msgid ""
"First, please check the [issue "
"tracker](https://github.com/okfn/opendataeditor/issues). Look for issues "
"with “help wanted” or “good first issue.” **If you want to submit a PR, "
"there needs to be a corresponding issue in the issue tracker.** Please "
"link the issue in your PR, and provide a brief explanation of the changes"
" you are pushing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:60
msgid "What is the review process for your contribution?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:62
msgid ""
"Your contribution will be **reviewed by the Open Data Editor core team at"
" Open Knowledge Foundation**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:64
msgid ""
"In case of documentation and code contributions, a member of the core "
"team will check if it is relevant, helpful, and easy to understand. If "
"small changes are needed, they suggest edits. Once everything looks good,"
" the contribution is approved and added to the project, and the "
"contributor is acknowledged (because every contribution matters\\!)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:66
msgid ""
"In case of bugs and feedback contributions, the core team will discuss if"
" and how they can be implemented. We can include you in the discussion if"
" you wish. Once we have a clear pathway, we will notify you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:68
msgid "Do you need help?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contribution-guidelines.md:70
msgid ""
"If at any point you need help, feel free to contact us via email at "
"[info@okfn.org](mailto:info@okfn.org)."
msgstr ""

